00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:56.210
So, now let's look at the other way.

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:57.880
How the 80/20 Rule

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:00.940
is often used in consulting
in similar industries.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:04.270
And this is for the internal
organization of work

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:06.840
for the prioritization of the team.

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:08.950
Also the time management, if you like.

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:10.430
And here the basic idea is,

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:12.170
that as with all the other things,

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:16.120
often 20% of the effort
of the work of a team

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:19.160
leads to 80% of the outcome.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.020
And this of course, the
other way round means

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:24.100
that the last 20% of output,

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:26.930
the last 20% of polishing something,

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:29.740
takes 80% of the whole time.

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:32.410
So here the basic question
is, is this really necessary?

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:34.640
Is this really required?

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:36.970
And of course, your the meme behavior

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:40.700
of a consulting partner is
to walk into the team room

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:43.950
and say something like,
"Hey, let's be 80/20."

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:47.490
But then he/she proposes
a super detailed analysis

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:49.150
which would take the whole team

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:51.130
weeks and month as really to complete,

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:52.760
with no understanding at all,

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:54.707
what is really absolutely required.

00:09:54.707 --> 00:09:56.870
And what is just a nice add on.

00:09:56.870 --> 00:09:58.810
So, often it's always
a little bit of a joke.

00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:01.420
Let's be 80/20 because unfortunately

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:02.660
or for whatever reason,

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:03.850
many many things,

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:07.280
many analysis that
consultants do, are not 80/20.

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:09.410
But there's often the big push

00:10:09.410 --> 00:10:13.180
to be extremely diligent,
to be extremely detailed.

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:15.630
And of course that might
be good reasons for that,

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:18.220
but still the whole idea is important,

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:21.600
and does afterward also play
a big role in consulting.

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:23.550
And it happens all the time

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:25.270
that for instance, as a new team

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:27.570
joining a new client for a new project,

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:30.070
there might be a business
with different business units,

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:31.730
five business units, for instance.

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:33.010
But then you might decide

00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:37.090
to only look into the biggest
two or three business units.

00:10:37.090 --> 00:10:39.150
And actually you might have lots of ideas,

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:41.010
lots of improvement potential

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:42.900
for business unit four and five.

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:45.100
But these business units are so small.

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:47.583
Even if you improve their profit by 20%,

00:10:47.583 --> 00:10:51.470
it's just such a little part
of the overall profit baseline

00:10:51.470 --> 00:10:52.303
for the company,

00:10:52.303 --> 00:10:54.520
that the impact would
just not be good enough.

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:56.240
And you would be much better off,

00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:58.950
if we really would focus on the
larger three business units.

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:00.560
And of course, considerations like that,

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:02.550
breakdown up to the activities

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:05.710
of really the most junior
people in the team room.

00:11:05.710 --> 00:11:07.620
So you might be a business analyst,

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:08.790
you're working on an analysis.

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:11.040
And you get some data from the client

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:12.140
and you do an analysis,

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:15.200
but then you realize that
certain pieces are missing.

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:17.650
The client did not provide the full data

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:19.780
of certain products,
certain business units,

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:22.110
whatever certain data
points are still not there.

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:24.120
And you of course, the
natural inclination is that,

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:25.130
yes, you need this.

00:11:25.130 --> 00:11:26.670
You might need to spend another week

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:28.040
to talk to another person

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:29.890
who can provide you
with this data as well.

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:31.840
With many many similar tasks

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:34.770
it's very easy to invest a lot of time

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:38.550
into really getting
something from 90% to 100%.

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:39.700
And you are just so important

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:42.010
to always have the bigger picture in mind.

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:44.900
Is this really helping you
to answer the questions

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:46.330
that you want to answer?

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:49.770
Or, aren't 80% or 90% of the information

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:52.770
not good enough to actually
get exactly these answers?

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:56.720
Is this additional 10-20%
of results really required?

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:58.000
Does this even help you at all?

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:00.063
So, if you'd like to
simplify it in the end

00:12:00.063 --> 00:12:02.450
being 80/20 means to be pragmatic.

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:04.380
To not over-complicate things.

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:05.780
To realize and understand

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:08.670
when what you have is just
good enough for what you need.

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:11.520
Or to use another meme coinciding phrase.

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:15.270
The opposite of being
80/20 is to boil the ocean,

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:16.793
but to get really everything done,

00:12:16.793 --> 00:12:19.203
to put as much energy into something

00:12:19.203 --> 00:12:21.650
that you will be able to
really boil the ocean.

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:24.910
So, ladies and gents, let's
not boil the ocean please,

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:27.640
but let's be a bit more 80/20 here.

